`a == NULL` (L669) | allocates, `hdr.length = 1`, elem0 zeroed, `capacity = 4` | `err_hmput_default_null` | [x] |\n| E15 | `stbds_hmput_default` | `a != NULL` **and** `hdr.length == 0` (L669) | re-grows / re-zeroes elem0, `hdr.length = 1` | `err_hmput_default_zero_length` | [x] |\n| E16 | `stbds_hmput_default` | `a != NULL` and `hdr.length != 0` | returns `a` unchanged, nothing written | `err_hmput_default_noop` | [x] |\n| E17 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `a == NULL` (L686) | allocates 1 zeroed elem, `hdr.length=1`, then proceeds to insert | `err_hmput_key_null_map` | [x] |\n| E18 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `hdr.hash_table == NULL` (L698) | new 8-slot index; `string.mode = (mode >= 1) ? SH_DEFAULT : 0` | `cfg` rows C10/C11 + `err_hmput_key_mode_selects_string_mode` | [x] |\n| E19 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `table->used_count >= table->used_count_threshold` (L698) | index doubles (`slot_count*2`), old index rehashed and freed | `err_hmput_grow_at_threshold` | [x] |\n| E20 | `stbds_hmput_key` | computed `hash < 2` (L719) — `hash == 0` or `1` | `hash += 2` so slots never collide with EMPTY(0)/DELETED(1) | `err_hash_below_2_bumped` (search for a seed producing hash<2 is infeasible → pinned indirectly by full-storage fingerprint equality over 10⁴ random keys) | [x] |\n| E21 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `mode` **out of enum range** (`2`, `7`, `INT_MAX`, i.e. `mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING`) (L713/L732) | treated as STRING: `stbds_hash_string`+`strcmp`, `temp_key` written | `err_mode_out_of_range_string_side` | [x] |\n| E22 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `mode` negative (`-1`, `INT_MIN`) | treated as BINARY: `stbds_hash_bytes`+`memcmp`, `string.mode = 0` | `err_mode_negative_is_binary` | [x] |\n| E23 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `table->string.mode` not in `{SH_STRDUP,SH_ARENA,SH_DEFAULT}` (switch `default:`, L789) — e.g. `SH_NONE(0)` or a truncated out-of-range `shmode_func` mode | `memcpy(elem, key, keysize)` (raw key **bytes**, not a pointer) | `err_string_mode_default_branch` | [x] |\n| E24 | `stbds_hmput_key` | duplicate key hit in the *wrapped* half of a bucket (L747-751) | `temp = index`, **`temp_key` NOT updated** (asymmetry vs. L732) | `err_dup_key_wrapped_half_no_temp_key` | [x] |\n| E25 | `stbds_hmput_key` | a tombstone was seen before the empty slot (`tombstone >= 0`, L766) | insert goes into the tombstone slot, `--tombstone_count` | `err_insert_reuses_tombstone` | [x] |\n| E26 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `a == NULL` (L809) | returns `0` (**NULL**) | `err_hmdel_null_map` | [x] |\n| E27 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `hdr.hash_table == 0` (L816) | `temp = 0`, returns `a` unchanged | `err_hmdel_no_table` | [x] |\n| E28 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | key not found (`slot < 0`, L821) | `temp = 0`, returns `a`, length/used_count unchanged | `err_hmdel_missing_key` | [x] |\n| E29 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | key found | `temp = 1`, `hash[i]=STBDS_HASH_DELETED(1)`, `index[i]=STBDS_INDEX_DELETED(-2)`, `--used_count`, `++tombstone_count`, `--hdr.length` | `err_hmdel_found_sets_temp1` | [x] |\n| E30 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` **exactly** and `string.mode == SH_STRDUP` (L836) | frees the key; note `mode == 2` (also \"string\" for hashing) does **not** free | `err_hmdel_strdup_free_only_mode_1` | [x] |\n| E31 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | deleted element is the last one (`old_index == final_index`, L839) | no `memmove`, no slot re-point | `err_hmdel_last_element` | [x] |\n| E32 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `used_count < used_count_shrink_threshold && slot_count > 8` (L854) | index shrinks to `slot_count>>1`, old freed | `err_hmdel_shrink` | [x] |\n| E33 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `tombstone_count > tombstone_count_threshold` (L858) — for an 8-slot index the threshold is `1`, so the **2nd** tombstone | index rebuilt at the same `slot_count`, tombstones dropped | `err_hmdel_rebuild_on_tombstones` | [x] |\n| E34 | `stbds_shmode_func` | `mode` out of enum range (`0`, `4`, `44`, `300`, `-1`, `INT_MIN`) | `string.mode = (unsigned char) mode` — silently truncated (`300 → 44`), later hits the switch `default:` | `err_shmode_out_of_range` | [x] |\n| E35 | `stbds_stralloc` | `len > a->remaining` and `len > blocksize` (L893) | dedicated block spliced *after* head (or becomes head with `remaining = 0`), returns `sb->storage` | `err_stralloc_oversized_string` | [x] |\n| E36 | `stbds_stralloc` | `a->storage == NULL` on the oversized path (L899) | `sb->next = 0; a->storage = sb; a->remaining = 0` | `err_stralloc_oversized_empty_arena` | [x] |\n| E37 | `stbds_stralloc` | `blocksize >= STBDS_STRING_ARENA_BLOCKSIZE_MAX (1<<20)` (L890) | `a->block` stops incrementing (saturates at 22) | `err_stralloc_block_saturates` | [x] |\n| E38 | `stbds_stralloc` | `a->block >= 128` → shift count `>= 64` in `512 << (block>>1)` | x86-64 `shl %cl` masks the count to 6 bits (verified in the C disassembly): `512 << ((block>>1) & 63)`; e.g. `block=250 → blocksize 0` → oversized path | `err_stralloc_huge_block_masked_shift` | [x] |\n| E39 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len == 0` (and `p == NULL`) | no byte is read; `switch(0)` → `break`; returns the length-only siphash | `err_hash_bytes_null_zero_len` | [x] |\n| E40 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len % 8 == 1..7` (tail `switch`, L532) | fall-through accumulates `d[0..len%8-1]`; `d[3]<<24` **sign-extends** into `size_t` | `err_hash_bytes_tail_sign_extension` | [x] |\n| E41 | `stbds_hash_string` | empty string `\"\"` | loop body never runs; finaliser applied to `seed` | `err_hash_string_empty` | [x] |\n| E42 | `stbds_is_key_equal` | `mode >= 1` with a *binary*-populated table | `strcmp` on the first 8 bytes of the element read as a `char*` → garbage deref (undefined in C, crashes both) | documented, **not executed** (UB, address dependent) | [x] |\n| E43 | `strkey` | `n = INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `0`, negative | `sprintf(buffer,\"test_%d\",n)` — 16 bytes worst case, fits the 256-byte static buffer | `err_strkey_extremes` (in `tests/demo_diff.rs`) | [x] |\n| E44 | `helxo` | `letter = 0` / `-128` / `127` / `200`-as-`char` | `%c` of a `char` promoted to `int`; `0` emits a NUL byte, `-128` emits byte `0x80` | `helxo_letters` (in `tests/demo_diff.rs`) | [x] |\n\n## `assert` rows (live in the shipped C `.so`; abort the process on failure)\n\n`STBDS_ASSERT` is `assert` and the C library is built **without** `NDEBUG`.\nA failing assert calls `__assert_fail` → `abort()`.  The Rust translation\ncompiles `stbds_assert!` to a no-op, which is only observable if an assert can\nactually fail.  Rows A1..A7 below record every assert and why it is\nunreachable through the public API (so no observable divergence exists).  None\nis executed by the test suite — a fired C assert would kill the test process\nand prove nothing about the Rust side.\n\n| # | function | assert | reachable from the public API? |\n|---|----------|--------|--------------------------------|\n| A1 | `stbds_make_hash_index` L401 | `used_count_threshold + tombstone_count_threshold < slot_count` | No: `slot_count` is only ever `8`, `slot_count*2` or `slot_count>>1` (bounded below by 8) → `6+1 < 8` … `3n/4 + 3n/16 < n`. Static fn, not exported. |\n| A2 | `stbds_hmput_key` L778 | `(size_t)i+1 <= stbds_arrcap(a)` | No: guarded by the `if` on L774 which grows the array first. |\n| A3 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L828 | `slot < (ptrdiff_t) table->slot_count` | No: `stbds_hm_find_slot` masks `pos` with `slot_count-1`. |\n| A4 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L832 | `table->used_count >= 0` | Never fails: `used_count` is `size_t` (always `>= 0`); tautology. |\n| A5 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L846 | `slot >= 0` (re-find of the moved last element) | Only with a *mode-mismatched* re-find (e.g. `mode == 2` + string keys, where L842 takes the binary branch and hashes the pointer bytes) — address dependent ⇒ not comparable, excluded from the suite (same class as E42). |\n| A6 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L849 | `b->index[i] == final_index` | Same as A5. |\n| A7 | `stbds_stralloc` L913 | `len <= a->remaining` | No: the `if` on L885 guarantees it, unless the caller hands in a corrupt arena (`remaining` large, `storage == NULL` → NULL deref before the assert). |\n\n## Generic FFI boundary rows (required by Phase C even though not in the C source)\n\n| # | condition | expected C result | test | ✔ |\n|---|-----------|-------------------|------|---|\n| G1 | NULL map pointer into every entry point that documents it (`arrgrowf`, `hmfree_func`, `hmget_key`, `hmget_key_ts`, `hmput_default`, `hmput_key`, `hmdel_key`) | see E1..E28 | `err_all_null_map_entry_points` | [x] |\n| G2 | NULL data pointer + `len == 0` into `stbds_hash_bytes` | pure function of `len`/`seed` | `err_hash_bytes_null_zero_len` | [x] |\n| G3 | `keysize == 0` into `hmput_key`/`hmget_key`/`hmdel_key` (binary mode) | `memcmp(...,0) == 0` → **every** key compares equal; hash of 0 bytes is a constant → single slot ever used | `err_keysize_zero` | [x] |\n| G4 | `keysize` larger than `elemsize` (overlapping writes) | `memcpy` overruns the element into the next one (defined, deterministic) | `err_keysize_gt_elemsize` | [x] |\n| G5 | oversized `len`/`elemsize` (`SIZE_MAX`, `SIZE_MAX/2`) into `arrgrowf` | unsigned wraparound, see E4/E5 | `err_arrgrowf_size_overflow_wraps` | [x] |\n| G6 | out-of-range `mode` **enum** values across the FFI boundary: `-2147483648`, `-1`, `0`, `1`, `2`, `3`, `44`, `2147483647` into `hmput_key`/`hmget_key`/`hmget_key_ts`/`hmdel_key` | `>= 1` ⇒ string side, `<= 0` ⇒ binary side; `hmdel_key`'s strdup-free and key-reload use `== 1` **exactly** | `err_mode_matrix_binary`, `err_mode_out_of_range_string_side`, `err_mode_negative_is_binary` | [x] |\n| G7 | out-of-range `shmode_func` mode enum (`STBDS_SH_*` is `0..3`): `4`, `44`, `255`, `256`, `300`, `-1`, `INT_MIN` | `(unsigned char)` truncation, then switch `default:` | `err_shmode_out_of_range` | [x] |\n| G8 | one step past a valid range: insert exactly `used_count_threshold` (6 of 8 slots) then one more | growth on the **6th** insert (`>=`, not `>`) | `err_hmput_grow_at_threshold` | [x] |\n| G9 | one step past the tombstone threshold (`tombstone_count_threshold == 1` for 8 slots) | rebuild on the 2nd delete | `err_hmdel_rebuild_on_tombstones` | [x] |\n| G10 | `elemsize == 0` into `hmput_key` (degenerate) | `arrgrowf(0,0,0,1)` → 32-byte alloc; `arr_to_hash` == `arr`; every element aliases | documented, **not executed** (aliases the header ⇒ corrupts `hdr` identically in both, but the `memcpy` target overlaps the header and the result is address/allocator dependent) | [x] |\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
