es_tail_sign_extension` | [x] |","-| E41 | `stbds_hash_string` | empty string `\"\"` | loop body never runs; finaliser applied to `seed` | `err_hash_string_empty` | [x] |","-| E42 | `stbds_is_key_equal` | `mode >= 1` with a *binary*-populated table | `strcmp` on the first 8 bytes of the element read as a `char*` → garbage deref (undefined in C, crashes both) | documented, **not executed** (UB, address dependent) | [x] |","-| E43 | `strkey` | `n = INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `0`, negative | `sprintf(buffer,\"test_%d\",n)` — 16 bytes worst case, fits the 256-byte static buffer | `err_strkey_extremes` (in `tests/demo_diff.rs`) | [x] |","-| E44 | `helxo` | `letter = 0` / `-128` / `127` / `200`-as-`char` | `%c` of a `char` promoted to `int`; `0` emits a NUL byte, `-128` emits byte `0x80` | `helxo_letters` (in `tests/demo_diff.rs`) | [x] |","+| E28 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | key not found (`slot < 0`, L821) | `temp = 0`, returns `a`, map otherwise untouched | `err_hmdel_missing_found_and_last` | [x] |","+| E29 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | key found | `temp = 1`, `hash[i]=1`, `index[i]=-2`, `--used_count`, `++tombstone_count`, `--hdr.length` | `err_hmdel_missing_found_and_last` | [x] |","+| E30 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` **exactly** && `string.mode == SH_STRDUP` (L836) | frees the key; with `mode = 2` (also \"string\" for hashing) the key is **not** freed — verified by reading the vacated slot's still-intact string | `err_hmdel_strdup_free_only_mode_1` | [x] |","+| E31 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `old_index == final_index` (L839) | no `memmove`, no slot re-point, survivors keep their indices | `err_hmdel_missing_found_and_last`, `cfg_del_last` | [x] |","+| E32 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `used_count < used_count_shrink_threshold && slot_count > 8` (L854) | index halves (16→8 on the 4th of 7 deletes: `4 < 4` is false, `3 < 4` is true) | `err_hmdel_shrink` | [x] |","+| E33 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `tombstone_count > tombstone_count_threshold` (L858) — `1` for an 8-slot index | rebuild at the same size on the **2nd** tombstone, tombstones dropped | `err_hmdel_rebuild_on_tombstones` | [x] |","+| E34 | `stbds_shmode_func` | `mode` out of enum range (`4, 5, 44, 127, 128, 255, 256, 257, 300, -1, -256, INT_MIN, INT_MAX`) | `string.mode = (unsigned char) mode` — silent truncation (`300 → 44`, `256 → 0`) | `err_shmode_out_of_range` | [x] |","+| E35 | `stbds_stralloc` | `len > a->remaining` **and** `len > blocksize` (L893) | dedicated block; spliced *after* the head when one exists | `err_stralloc_oversized_string` | [x] |","+| E36 | `stbds_stralloc` | same, but `a->storage == NULL` (L899) | `sb->next = 0; a->storage = sb; a->remaining = 0` | `err_stralloc_oversized_empty_arena` | [x] |","+| E37 | `stbds_stralloc` | `blocksize >= STBDS_STRING_ARENA_BLOCKSIZE_MAX (1<<20)` (L890) | `a->block` stops incrementing (checked for block 0,1,2,19..25) | `err_stralloc_block_saturates` | [x] |","+| E38 | `stbds_stralloc` | `a->block >= 110` → `512 << (block>>1)` overflows to 0; `block >= 128` → shift count > 63 | x86-64 `shl %cl` masks the count to 6 bits (verified in the C disassembly): `512 << ((block>>1) & 63)`; blocksize 0 ⇒ dedicated-block path. Rust uses `wrapping_shl` to match. Checked for block 110,111,126..131,250,254,255 | `err_stralloc_huge_block_masked_shift` | [x] |","+| E39 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len == 0` (with `p == NULL` **and** `p != NULL`) | no byte read; `switch(0)` → `break`; value depends only on `len`/`seed` | `err_hash_bytes_null_zero_len` | [x] |","+| E40 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len - i ∈ 1..7` (tail `switch`, L532) | fall-through accumulation; `d[3]<<24` / `d[7]<<24` **sign-extend** into `size_t` | `err_hash_bytes_tail_sign_extension`, `cfg_hash_bytes_high_bit_patterns` | [x] |","+| E41 | `stbds_hash_string` | empty string `\"\"` | loop skipped, finaliser applied to `seed` (64 random seeds + extremes) | `err_hash_string_empty` | [x] |","+| E43 | `strkey` | `n = 0, ±1, ±9/10, 99/100, INT_MAX, INT_MIN, INT_MAX-1, INT_MIN+1`, 256 random | `sprintf(buffer,\"test_%d\",n)`; worst case 17 bytes fits the 256-byte static buffer; the returned address is stable | `cfg_strkey_matrix` (`tests/demo_diff.rs`) | [x] |","+| E44 | `helxo` | `letter = 0, -1, -128, 127, 200-as-char, '\\n', '%', '\\t'` + 64 random | `%c` of a `char` promoted to `int`: `0` emits a NUL byte, `-128` emits `0x80`; stdout compared byte for byte | `cfg_helxo_letters` (`tests/demo_diff.rs`) | [x] |"," ","-## `assert` rows (live in the shipped C `.so`; abort the process on failure)","+## Rows that are provably NOT executable (documented, not faked)"," ","-`STBDS_ASSERT` is `assert` and the C library is built **without** `NDEBUG`.","-A failing assert calls `__assert_fail` → `abort()`.  The Rust translation","-compiles `stbds_assert!` to a no-op, which is only observable if an assert can","-actually fail.  Rows A1..A7 below record every assert and why it is","-unreachable through the public API (so no observable divergence exists).  None","-is executed by the test suite — a fired C assert would kill the test process","-and prove nothing about the Rust side.","+| # | condition | why it cannot be tested |","+|---|-----------|-------------------------|","+| E42 | `stbds_is_key_equal` with `mode >= 1` on a *binary*-populated element | `strcmp` dereferences the element's first 8 bytes as a `char *` → wild pointer. Undefined in C and address dependent, so \"same behaviour\" is not observable. Reachable only by mixing modes on one map; excluded from the suite. |","+| E38b | `stbds_stralloc` with `a->block` such that `512 << ((block>>1)&63)` is huge but non-zero (e.g. 109 → 2⁶³, 200 → 2⁴⁵) | the C `malloc` fails and the *next* statement dereferences the NULL result → SIGSEGV in **both** libraries; the test process cannot survive it. |","+| G10 | `elemsize == 0` into `hmput_key` | `arr_to_hash(a,0) == a`, so every element aliases the header; the resulting corruption is allocator/address dependent. |","+| — | `stbds_arrfreef(NULL)` | computes `free((char*)NULL - 32)` → invalid free / abort in **both** libraries. Exercised nowhere; `tests/array_diff.rs` explicitly guards against it (with a comment). |"," ","+## `assert` rows (live in the shipped C `.so`, `abort()` on failure)","+","+`STBDS_ASSERT` is `assert` and the C `.so` is built without `NDEBUG` (it imports","+`__assert_fail`).  The Rust translation compiles `stbds_assert!` to a no-op,","+which is only observable if an assert can actually fail — the table below shows","+that none can be reached through the public API, so no divergence exists.  None","+is executed: a fired C assert would kill the test process and prove nothing","+about the Rust side.","+"," | # | function | assert | reachable from the public API? |"," |---|----------|--------|--------------------------------|","-| A1 | `stbds_make_hash_index` L401 | `used_count_threshold + tombstone_count_threshold < slot_count` | No: `slot_count` is only ever `8`, `slot_count*2` or `slot_count>>1` (bounded below by 8) → `6+1 < 8` … `3n/4 + 3n/16 < n`. Static fn, not exported. |","-| A2 | `stbds_hmput_key` L778 | `(size_t)i+1 <= stbds_arrcap(a)` | No: guarded by the `if` on L774 which grows the array first. |","+| A1 | `stbds_make_hash_index` L401 | `used_count_threshold + tombstone_count_threshold < slot_count` | No. `slot_count` is only ever `8`, `slot_count*2` or `slot_count>>1` (floored at 8) ⇒ `3n/4 + 3n/16 < n` holds for every `n >= 8`. Static function, not exported. |","+| A2 | `stbds_hmput_key` L778 | `(size_t) i+1 <= stbds_arrcap(a)` | No: the `if` on L774 grows the array first. |"," | A3 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L828 | `slot < (ptrdiff_t) table->slot_count` | No: `stbds_hm_find_slot` masks `pos` with `slot_count-1`. |","-| A4 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L832 | `table->used_count >= 0` | Never fails: `used_count` is `size_t` (always `>= 0`); tautology. |","-| A5 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L846 | `slot >= 0` (re-find of the moved last element) | Only with a *mode-mismatched* re-find (e.g. `mode == 2` + string keys, where L842 takes the binary branch and hashes the pointer bytes) — address dependent ⇒ not comparable, excluded from the suite (same class as E42). |","+| A4 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L832 | `table->used_count >= 0` | Tautology (`size_t`). |","+| A5 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L846 | `slot >= 0` after the re-find of the moved last element | Only with a mode-mismatched re-find (`mode >= 2` + string keys makes L842 take the *binary* branch and hash the key **pointer bytes**) — address dependent, same class as E42. The suite therefore deletes only the *last* element for `mode != 1` (see `err_mode_matrix_binary`). |"," | A6 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L849 | `b->index[i] == final_index` | Same as A5. |","-| A7 | `stbds_stralloc` L913 | `len <= a->remaining` | No: the `if` on L885 guarantees it, unless the caller hands in a corrupt arena (`remaining` large, `storage == NULL` → NULL deref before the assert). |","+| A7 | `stbds_stralloc` L913 | `len <= a->remaining` | No: the `if` on L885 guarantees it (a corrupt arena with `remaining > 0, storage == NULL` NULL-derefs before reaching the assert, in both libraries). |"," ","-## Generic FFI boundary rows (required by Phase C even though not in the C source)","+## Generic FFI-boundary rows (required by Phase C)"," "," | # | condition | expected C result | test | ✔ |"," |---|-----------|-------------------|------|---|","-| G1 | NULL map pointer into every entry point that documents it (`arrgrowf`, `hmfree_func`, `hmget_key`, `hmget_key_ts`, `hmput_default`, `hmput_key`, `hmdel_key`) | see E1..E28 | `err_all_null_map_entry_points` | [x] |","+| G1 | NULL map pointer into every entry point that takes one (`arrgrowf`, `hmfree_func`, `hmget_key`, `hmget_key_ts`, `hmput_default`, `hmput_key`, `hmdel_key`) | see E1..E28 | `err_all_null_map_entry_points` | [x] |"," | G2 | NULL data pointer + `len == 0` into `stbds_hash_bytes` | pure function of `len`/`seed` | `err_hash_bytes_null_zero_len` | [x] |","-| G3 | `keysize == 0` into `hmput_key`/`hmget_key`/`hmdel_key` (binary mode) | `memcmp(...,0) == 0` → **every** key compares equal; hash of 0 bytes is a constant → single slot ever used | `err_keysize_zero` | [x] |","-| G4 | `keysize` larger than `elemsize` (overlapping writes) | `memcpy` overruns the element into the next one (defined, deterministic) | `err_keysize_gt_elemsize` | [x] |","-| G5 | oversized `len`/`elemsize` (`SIZE_MAX`, `SIZE_MAX/2`) into `arrgrowf` | unsigned wraparound, see E4/E5 | `err_arrgrowf_size_overflow_wraps` | [x] |","-| G6 | out-of-range `mode` **enum** values across the FFI boundary: `-2147483648`, `-1`, `0`, `1`, `2`, `3`, `44`, `2147483647` into `hmput_key`/`hmget_key`/`hmget_key_ts`/`hmdel_key` | `>= 1` ⇒ string side, `<= 0` ⇒ binary side; `hmdel_key`'s strdup-free and key-reload use `== 1` **exactly** | `err_mode_matrix_binary`, `err_mode_out_of_range_string_side`, `err_mode_negative_is_binary` | [x] |","-| G7 | out-of-range `shmode_func` mode enum (`STBDS_SH_*` is `0..3`): `4`, `44`, `255`, `256`, `300`, `-1`, `INT_MIN` | `(unsigned char)` truncation, then switch `default:` | `err_shmode_out_of_range` | [x] |","-| G8 | one step past a valid range: insert exactly `used_count_threshold` (6 of 8 slots) then one more | growth on the **6th** insert (`>=`, not `>`) | `err_hmput_grow_at_threshold` | [x] |","-| G9 | one step past the tombstone threshold (`tombstone_count_threshold == 1` for 8 slots) | rebuild on the 2nd delete | `err_hmdel_rebuild_on_tombstones` | [x] |","-| G10 | `elemsize == 0` into `hmput_key` (degenerate) | `arrgrowf(0,0,0,1)` → 32-byte alloc; `arr_to_hash` == `arr`; every element aliases | documented, **not executed** (aliases the header ⇒ corrupts `hdr` identically in both, but the `memcpy` target overlaps the header and the result is address/allocator dependent) | [x] |","+| G3 | `keysize == 0` (binary mode) | `memcmp(...,0) == 0` ⇒ *every* key compares equal; the map can only hold one entry; one delete empties it | `err_keysize_zero` | [x] |","+| G4 | `keysize > elemsize` | the `memcpy` overruns into the next element (deterministic); the clobbered key becomes unfindable in both libraries | `err_keysize_gt_elemsize` | [x] |","+| G5 | oversized `elemsize`/`addlen` (`SIZE_MAX`, `SIZE_MAX/2`) | unsigned wraparound (E4/E5) | `err_arrgrowf_size_overflow_wraps`, `err_arrgrowf_addlen_overflow` | [x] |","+| G6 | out-of-range `mode` **enum** values across FFI (`INT_MIN, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 44, 1000, INT_MAX`) through `hmput_key`/`hmget_key`/`hmget_key_ts`/`hmdel_key` | `>= 1` ⇒ string side, `<= 0` ⇒ binary side; `hmdel_key`'s strdup-free uses `== 1` exactly | `err_mode_matrix_binary`, `err_mode_out_of_range_string_side`, `err_mode_negative_is_binary`, `err_hmdel_strdup_free_only_mode_1` | [x] |","+| G7 | out-of-range `shmode_func` enum (valid range is `0..3`) | `(unsigned char)` truncation, then switch `default:` | `err_shmode_out_of_range` | [x] |","+| G8 | one step past the growth threshold (6 vs 7 inserts on an 8-slot index) | growth on the 7th (`>=`, evaluated *before* the increment) | `err_hmput_grow_at_threshold` | [x] |","+| G9 | one step past the tombstone threshold (`== 1` for 8 slots) and the shrink threshold | rebuild on the 2nd delete; shrink when `used_count` drops *below* `slot_count>>2` | `err_hmdel_rebuild_on_tombstones`, `err_hmdel_shrink` | [x] |"]}],"originalFile":"# ERRORS.md — Phase A error / rejection surface table\n\nDerived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c` by grepping every `return`,\n`STBDS_ASSERT`, `== NULL` / `!= NULL` / `== 0` / `< 0` / `>= …` guard and every\nmin/max constant.  `stb_ds` has no error *enum*: it rejects input by returning\na sentinel (`-1` = `STBDS_INDEX_EMPTY`, `NULL`/`0`), by taking an early-out\nbranch, or by tripping an `assert` (asserts are **live** — the C `.so` imports\n`__assert_fail`, i.e. `NDEBUG` is not defined).\n\nLegend for \"expected C result\":\n* `temp` = `stbds_header(raw_array)->temp` (the value the `stbds_hm*` macros\n  read back).\n* `hdr` = `stbds_array_header` in front of the raw array.\n\nTest column: name of the differential test that pins the row\n(`tests/errors_diff.rs` unless stated otherwise).\n\n## Sentinel / early-return rows\n\n| # | function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test | ✔ |\n|---|----------|------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|---|\n| E1 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | `min_cap <= stbds_arrcap(a)` and `arrlen(a)+addlen <= min_cap` (L286) | returns `a` **unchanged**, no realloc, header untouched | `err_arrgrowf_no_grow_returns_same_ptr` | [x] |\n| E2 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | `a == NULL` (L300) | fresh alloc, `hdr.length=0`, `hdr.hash_table=0`, `hdr.temp=0`, `hdr.capacity=max(min_cap,4)` | `err_arrgrowf_null_input` | [x] |\n| E3 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | `min_cap < 4` after the `min_len` fixup and `2*cap` fixup (L291) | capacity bumped to exactly `4` | `err_arrgrowf_min_cap_below_4` | [x] |\n| E4 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | `elemsize*min_cap + 32` overflows `size_t` (`elemsize = SIZE_MAX/2`) | wraps (unsigned), `realloc` of the wrapped size, `capacity = 4` | `err_arrgrowf_size_overflow_wraps` | [x] |\n| E5 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | `addlen` makes `min_len` wrap (`arrlen + addlen`, L280, `addlen = SIZE_MAX`) | `min_len` wraps; `min_cap` follows the wrapped value | `err_arrgrowf_addlen_overflow` | [x] |\n| E6 | `stbds_hmfree_func` | `a == NULL` (L573) | returns immediately, no free, no crash | `err_hmfree_null` | [x] |\n| E7 | `stbds_hmfree_func` | `a != NULL` but `hdr.hash_table == NULL` (L574) | skips the strdup-key loop and `strreset`, frees `hash_table`(NULL) + header | `err_hmfree_no_table` | [x] |\n| E8 | `stbds_hm_find_slot` | key absent: first probed slot with `hash == STBDS_HASH_EMPTY(0)` in the *upper* half of the bucket (L609) | returns `-1` | `err_get_missing_key_returns_minus1` | [x] |\n| E9 | `stbds_hm_find_slot` | key absent: `hash == 0` found in the *wrapped* (`i < limit`) half of the bucket (L620) | returns `-1` | `err_get_missing_key_wrapped_half` | [x] |\n| E10 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | `a == NULL` (L634) | allocates a 1-elem zeroed array, `*temp = STBDS_INDEX_EMPTY (-1)`, returns `arr+elemsize` (non-NULL), `hdr.length==1`, `hdr.capacity==4` | `err_hmget_ts_null_map` | [x] |\n| E11 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | `a != NULL`, `hdr.hash_table == 0` (L644) | `*temp = -1`, returns `a` unchanged | `err_hmget_ts_no_table` | [x] |\n| E12 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | `stbds_hm_find_slot` returned `< 0` (L648) | `*temp = STBDS_INDEX_EMPTY (-1)` | `err_get_missing_key_returns_minus1` | [x] |\n| E13 | `stbds_hmget_key` | any of E10..E12 | same as `*temp`, additionally stored into `stbds_header(ret-elemsize)->temp` | `err_hmget_key_writes_temp` | [x] |\n| E14 | `stbds_hmput_default` | `a == NULL` (L669) | allocates, `hdr.length = 1`, elem0 zeroed, `capacity = 4` | `err_hmput_default_null` | [x] |\n| E15 | `stbds_hmput_default` | `a != NULL` **and** `hdr.length == 0` (L669) | re-grows / re-zeroes elem0, `hdr.length = 1` | `err_hmput_default_zero_length` | [x] |\n| E16 | `stbds_hmput_default` | `a != NULL` and `hdr.length != 0` | returns `a` unchanged, nothing written | `err_hmput_default_noop` | [x] |\n| E17 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `a == NULL` (L686) | allocates 1 zeroed elem, `hdr.length=1`, then proceeds to insert | `err_hmput_key_null_map` | [x] |\n| E18 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `hdr.hash_table == NULL` (L698) | new 8-slot index; `string.mode = (mode >= 1) ? SH_DEFAULT : 0` | `cfg` rows C10/C11 + `err_hmput_key_mode_selects_string_mode` | [x] |\n| E19 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `table->used_count >= table->used_count_threshold` (L698) | index doubles (`slot_count*2`), old index rehashed and freed | `err_hmput_grow_at_threshold` | [x] |\n| E20 | `stbds_hmput_key` | computed `hash < 2` (L719) — `hash == 0` or `1` | `hash += 2` so slots never collide with EMPTY(0)/DELETED(1) | `err_hash_below_2_bumped` (search for a seed producing hash<2 is infeasible → pinned indirectly by full-storage fingerprint equality over 10⁴ random keys) | [x] |\n| E21 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `mode` **out of enum range** (`2`, `7`, `INT_MAX`, i.e. `mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING`) (L713/L732) | treated as STRING: `stbds_hash_string`+`strcmp`, `temp_key` written | `err_mode_out_of_range_string_side` | [x] |\n| E22 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `mode` negative (`-1`, `INT_MIN`) | treated as BINARY: `stbds_hash_bytes`+`memcmp`, `string.mode = 0` | `err_mode_negative_is_binary` | [x] |\n| E23 | `stbds_hmput_key` | `table->string.mode` not in `{SH_STRDUP,SH_ARENA,SH_DEFAULT}` (switch `default:`, L789) — e.g. `SH_NONE(0)` or a truncated out-of-range `shmode_func` mode | `memcpy(elem, key, keysize)` (raw key **bytes**, not a pointer) | `err_string_mode_default_branch` | [x] |\n| E24 | `stbds_hmput_key` | duplicate key hit in the *wrapped* half of a bucket (L747-751) | `temp = index`, **`temp_key` NOT updated** (asymmetry vs. L732) | `err_dup_key_wrapped_half_no_temp_key` | [x] |\n| E25 | `stbds_hmput_key` | a tombstone was seen before the empty slot (`tombstone >= 0`, L766) | insert goes into the tombstone slot, `--tombstone_count` | `err_insert_reuses_tombstone` | [x] |\n| E26 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `a == NULL` (L809) | returns `0` (**NULL**) | `err_hmdel_null_map` | [x] |\n| E27 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `hdr.hash_table == 0` (L816) | `temp = 0`, returns `a` unchanged | `err_hmdel_no_table` | [x] |\n| E28 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | key not found (`slot < 0`, L821) | `temp = 0`, returns `a`, length/used_count unchanged | `err_hmdel_missing_key` | [x] |\n| E29 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | key found | `temp = 1`, `hash[i]=STBDS_HASH_DELETED(1)`, `index[i]=STBDS_INDEX_DELETED(-2)`, `--used_count`, `++tombstone_count`, `--hdr.length` | `err_hmdel_found_sets_temp1` | [x] |\n| E30 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` **exactly** and `string.mode == SH_STRDUP` (L836) | frees the key; note `mode == 2` (also \"string\" for hashing) does **not** free | `err_hmdel_strdup_free_only_mode_1` | [x] |\n| E31 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | deleted element is the last one (`old_index == final_index`, L839) | no `memmove`, no slot re-point | `err_hmdel_last_element` | [x] |\n| E32 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `used_count < used_count_shrink_threshold && slot_count > 8` (L854) | index shrinks to `slot_count>>1`, old freed | `err_hmdel_shrink` | [x] |\n| E33 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | `tombstone_count > tombstone_count_threshold` (L858) — for an 8-slot index the threshold is `1`, so the **2nd** tombstone | index rebuilt at the same `slot_count`, tombstones dropped | `err_hmdel_rebuild_on_tombstones` | [x] |\n| E34 | `stbds_shmode_func` | `mode` out of enum range (`0`, `4`, `44`, `300`, `-1`, `INT_MIN`) | `string.mode = (unsigned char) mode` — silently truncated (`300 → 44`), later hits the switch `default:` | `err_shmode_out_of_range` | [x] |\n| E35 | `stbds_stralloc` | `len > a->remaining` and `len > blocksize` (L893) | dedicated block spliced *after* head (or becomes head with `remaining = 0`), returns `sb->storage` | `err_stralloc_oversized_string` | [x] |\n| E36 | `stbds_stralloc` | `a->storage == NULL` on the oversized path (L899) | `sb->next = 0; a->storage = sb; a->remaining = 0` | `err_stralloc_oversized_empty_arena` | [x] |\n| E37 | `stbds_stralloc` | `blocksize >= STBDS_STRING_ARENA_BLOCKSIZE_MAX (1<<20)` (L890) | `a->block` stops incrementing (saturates at 22) | `err_stralloc_block_saturates` | [x] |\n| E38 | `stbds_stralloc` | `a->block >= 128` → shift count `>= 64` in `512 << (block>>1)` | x86-64 `shl %cl` masks the count to 6 bits (verified in the C disassembly): `512 << ((block>>1) & 63)`; e.g. `block=250 → blocksize 0` → oversized path | `err_stralloc_huge_block_masked_shift` | [x] |\n| E39 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len == 0` (and `p == NULL`) | no byte is read; `switch(0)` → `break`; returns the length-only siphash | `err_hash_bytes_null_zero_len` | [x] |\n| E40 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len % 8 == 1..7` (tail `switch`, L532) | fall-through accumulates `d[0..len%8-1]`; `d[3]<<24` **sign-extends** into `size_t` | `err_hash_bytes_tail_sign_extension` | [x] |\n| E41 | `stbds_hash_string` | empty string `\"\"` | loop body never runs; finaliser applied to `seed` | `err_hash_string_empty` | [x] |\n| E42 | `stbds_is_key_equal` | `mode >= 1` with a *binary*-populated table | `strcmp` on the first 8 bytes of the element read as a `char*` → garbage deref (undefined in C, crashes both) | documented, **not executed** (UB, address dependent) | [x] |\n| E43 | `strkey` | `n = INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `0`, negative | `sprintf(buffer,\"test_%d\",n)` — 16 bytes worst case, fits the 256-byte static buffer | `err_strkey_extremes` (in `tests/demo_diff.rs`) | [x] |\n| E44 | `helxo` | `letter = 0` / `-128` / `127` / `200`-as-`char` | `%c` of a `char` promoted to `int`; `0` emits a NUL byte, `-128` emits byte `0x80` | `helxo_letters` (in `tests/demo_diff.rs`) | [x] |\n\n## `assert` rows (live in the shipped C `.so`; abort the process on failure)\n\n`STBDS_ASSERT` is `assert` and the C library is built **without** `NDEBUG`.\nA failing assert calls `__assert_fail` → `abort()`.  The Rust translation\ncompiles `stbds_assert!` to a no-op, which is only observable if an assert can\nactually fail.  Rows A1..A7 below record every assert and why it is\nunreachable through the public API (so no observable divergence exists).  None\nis executed by the test suite — a fired C assert would kill the test process\nand prove nothing about the Rust side.\n\n| # | function | assert | reachable from the public API? |\n|---|----------|--------|--------------------------------|\n| A1 | `stbds_make_hash_index` L401 | `used_count_threshold + tombstone_count_threshold < slot_count` | No: `slot_count` is only ever `8`, `slot_count*2` or `slot_count>>1` (bounded below by 8) → `6+1 < 8` … `3n/4 + 3n/16 < n`. Static fn, not exported. |\n| A2 | `stbds_hmput_key` L778 | `(size_t)i+1 <= stbds_arrcap(a)` | No: guarded by the `if` on L774 which grows the array first. |\n| A3 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L828 | `slot < (ptrdiff_t) table->slot_count` | No: `stbds_hm_find_slot` masks `pos` with `slot_count-1`. |\n| A4 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L832 | `table->used_count >= 0` | Never fails: `used_count` is `size_t` (always `>= 0`); tautology. |\n| A5 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L846 | `slot >= 0` (re-find of the moved last element) | Only with a *mode-mismatched* re-find (e.g. `mode == 2` + string keys, where L842 takes the binary branch and hashes the pointer bytes) — address dependent ⇒ not comparable, excluded from the suite (same class as E42). |\n| A6 | `stbds_hmdel_key` L849 | `b->index[i] == final_index` | Same as A5. |\n| A7 | `stbds_stralloc` L913 | `len <= a->remaining` | No: the `if` on L885 guarantees it, unless the caller hands in a corrupt arena (`remaining` large, `storage == NULL` → NULL deref before the assert). |\n\n## Generic FFI boundary rows (required by Phase C even though not in the C source)\n\n| # | condition | expected C result | test | ✔ |\n|---|-----------|-------------------|------|---|\n| G1 | NULL map pointer into every entry point that documents it (`arrgrowf`, `hmfree_func`, `hmget_key`, `hmget_key_ts`, `hmput_default`, `hmput_key`, `hmdel_key`) | see E1..E28 | `err_all_null_map_entry_points` | [x] |\n| G2 | NULL data pointer + `len == 0` into `stbds_hash_bytes` | pure function of `len`/`seed` | `err_hash_bytes_null_zero_len` | [x] |\n| G3 | `keysize == 0` into `hmput_key`/`hmget_key`/`hmdel_key` (binary mode) | `memcmp(...,0) == 0` → **every** key compares equal; hash of 0 bytes is a constant → single slot ever used | `err_keysize_zero` | [x] |\n| G4 | `keysize` larger than `elemsize` (overlapping writes) | `memcpy` overruns the element into the next one (defined, deterministic) | `err_keysize_gt_elemsize` | [x] |\n| G5 | oversized `len`/`elemsize` (`SIZE_MAX`, `SIZE_MAX/2`) into `arrgrowf` | unsigned wraparound, see E4/E5 | `err_arrgrowf_size_overflow_wraps` | [x] |\n| G6 | out-of-range `mode` **enum** values across the FFI boundary: `-2147483648`, `-1`, `0`, `1`, `2`, `3`, `44`, `2147483647` into `hmput_key`/`hmget_key`/`hmget_key_ts`/`hmdel_key` | `>= 1` ⇒ string side, `<= 0` ⇒ binary side; `hmdel_key`'s strdup-free and key-reload use `== 1` **exactly** | `err_mode_matrix_binary`, `err_mode_out_of_range_string_side`, `err_mode_negative_is_binary` | [x] |\n| G7 | out-of-range `shmode_func` mode enum (`STBDS_SH_*` is `0..3`): `4`, `44`, `255`, `256`, `300`, `-1`, `INT_MIN` | `(unsigned char)` truncation, then switch `default:` | `err_shmode_out_of_range` | [x] |\n| G8 | one step past a valid range: insert exactly `used_count_threshold` (6 of 8 slots) then one more | growth on the **6th** insert (`>=`, not `>`) | `err_hmput_grow_at_threshold` | [x] |\n| G9 | one step past the tombstone threshold (`tombstone_count_threshold == 1` for 8 slots) | rebuild on the 2nd delete | `err_hmdel_rebuild_on_tombstones` | [x] |\n| G10 | `elemsize == 0` into `hmput_key` (degenerate) | `arrgrowf(0,0,0,1)` → 32-byte alloc; `arr_to_hash` == `arr`; every element aliases | documented, **not executed** (aliases the header ⇒ corrupts `hdr` identically in both, but the `memcpy` target overlaps the header and the result is address/allocator dependent) | [x] |\n","userModified":false}}
