e shipped C compiles to `shl %cl` (mask 6 bits, confirmed by disassembly), where Rust would have panicked/aborted.\n- Unsigned wraparound parity: `wrapping_*` for `tombstone_count`/`used_count`/`length`/`slot_count*2`/`slot_count-1`/threshold and allocation-size arithmetic, so a corrupt-state call wraps exactly like C instead of panicking under `debug_assertions`.\n\n## Two harness bugs worth flagging\n- The fingerprint initially read one element past the array (the raw array's element 0 is the `(t)[-1]` default) — it found real uninitialized-memory reads.\n- **`cargo test --test X` does not rebuild a `cdylib`.** Mutation testing \"passed\" against a stale `.so`. `tests/common/mod.rs::assert_fresh` now aborts with `STALE cdylib` if the `.so` predates any `src/` file.\n\n## Phase D gate\n- [x] `nm -D` diff **empty** (16 = 16), no unresolved non-libc symbols — in *both* dev and release profiles.\n- [x] All 45 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass over randomized inputs.\n- [x] All 44 `ERRORS.md` rows have passing error-path tests (incl. out-of-range enum `mode`/`shmode` values, NULL pointers, zero/oversized lengths, one-past-threshold boundaries).\n- [x] Holds for the only feature combination, under dev, `--test-threads=1`, and release (`panic=abort`, no overflow checks).\n- [x] Suite proven sensitive: 22 behaviour-changing mutations injected → **all caught**; the 3 survivors were provably equivalent mutants (`min_cap <= 4` still assigns 4; `%i` == `%d`).\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (only the required `c_src/build/` output exists)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1318,"cache_read_input_tokens":313949,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1318,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4c73cdf-d3d2-480b-b64c-7f6e1f7b5869","uuid":"dfaa2799-9f70-4572-a18d-69380da4cf5d","timestamp":"2026-08-20T11